 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "65b24ff9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Practice Tasks"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cb6fe23c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Basic Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "1ace88e5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datasciencedojo/datasets/master/titanic.csv\"\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(url)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "79164255",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 1 — GroupBy basics"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "97ec85b4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Find the average fare paid by passengers in each embarkation port. Sort the result from highest to lowest."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "a873ca08",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Embarked\n",
       "C    59.954144\n",
       "S    27.079812\n",
       "Q    13.276030\n",
       "Name: Fare, dtype: float64"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 4,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df.groupby(\"Embarked\")[\"Fare\"].mean().sort_values(ascending=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1764bafc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 2 — .agg()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7010482c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Group by Sex and calculate in one .agg() call: average age, average fare, total number of passengers, and survival rate. Name your columns clearly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "4e4cae59",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/html": [
       "<div>\n",
       "<style scoped>\n",
       "    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n",
       "        vertical-align: middle;\n",
       "    }\n",
       "\n",
       "    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n",
       "        vertical-align: top;\n",
       "    }\n",
       "\n",
       "    .dataframe thead th {\n",
       "        text-align: right;\n",
       "    }\n",
       "</style>\n",
       "<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n",
       "  <thead>\n",
       "    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n",
       "      <th></th>\n",
       "      <th>avg_age</th>\n",
       "      <th>avg_fare</th>\n",
       "      <th>no_of_passengers</th>\n",
       "      <th>survival_rate</th>\n",
       "    </tr>\n",
       "    <tr>\n",
       "      <th>Sex</th>\n",
       "      <th></th>\n",
       "      <th></th>\n",
       "      <th></th>\n",
       "      <th></th>\n",
       "    </tr>\n",
       "  </thead>\n",
       "  <tbody>\n",
       "    <tr>\n",
       "      <th>female</th>\n",
       "      <td>27.915709</td>\n",
       "      <td>44.479818</td>\n",
       "      <td>314</td>\n",
       "      <td>0.742038</td>\n",
       "    </tr>\n",
       "    <tr>\n",
       "      <th>male</th>\n",
       "      <td>30.726645</td>\n",
       "      <td>25.523893</td>\n",
       "      <td>577</td>\n",
       "      <td>0.188908</td>\n",
       "    </tr>\n",
       "  </tbody>\n",
       "</table>\n",
       "</div>"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "          avg_age   avg_fare  no_of_passengers  survival_rate\n",
       "Sex                                                          \n",
       "female  27.915709  44.479818               314       0.742038\n",
       "male    30.726645  25.523893               577       0.188908"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 6,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df.groupby(\"Sex\").agg(\n",
    "    avg_age = (\"Age\" , \"mean\"),\n",
    "    avg_fare = (\"Fare\" , \"mean\"),\n",
    "    no_of_passengers = (\"PassengerId\" , \"count\"),\n",
    "    survival_rate = (\"Survived\" , \"mean\")\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0da4e777",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 3 — Multi-column groupby"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9bb5083f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Group by both Pclass and Survived. Find the average fare and average age for each combination. Reset the index and store as a clean DataFrame."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "485cc27c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "   Pclass  Survived       Fare        Age\n",
      "0       1         0  64.684007  43.695312\n",
      "1       1         1  95.608029  35.368197\n",
      "2       2         0  19.412328  33.544444\n",
      "3       2         1  22.055700  25.901566\n",
      "4       3         0  13.669364  26.555556\n",
      "5       3         1  13.694887  20.646118\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "result1 = df.groupby([\"Pclass\" , \"Survived\"])[[\"Fare\" , \"Age\"]].mean().reset_index()\n",
    "print(result1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a0b1ec9a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 4 — apply()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "837cae2d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "For each passenger class, find the age range (max age minus min age) using .apply() with a lambda."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "4aa74402",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Pclass\n",
       "1    79.08\n",
       "2    69.33\n",
       "3    73.58\n",
       "Name: Age, dtype: float64"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 11,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df.groupby(\"Pclass\")[\"Age\"].apply(lambda x : x.max() - x.min())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bca85ee9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 5 — merge()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "31315010",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Create these two DataFrames manually:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "472fdcff",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class_info = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Pclass\": [1, 2, 3],\n",
    "    \"class_name\": [\"First\", \"Second\", \"Third\"],\n",
    "    \"deck\": [\"A-E\", \"F\", \"G\"]\n",
    "})"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0d53c493",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Merge this with the Titanic DataFrame on Pclass. Then verify the merge worked by checking the shape and the new columns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "bd660724",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Shape: (891, 14)\n",
      "\n",
      "Columns:\n",
      "Index(['PassengerId', 'Survived', 'Pclass', 'Name', 'Sex', 'Age', 'SibSp',\n",
      "       'Parch', 'Ticket', 'Fare', 'Cabin', 'Embarked', 'class_name', 'deck'],\n",
      "      dtype='str')\n",
      "\n",
      "Preview:\n",
      "   Pclass class_name deck\n",
      "0       3      Third    G\n",
      "1       1      First  A-E\n",
      "2       3      Third    G\n",
      "3       1      First  A-E\n",
      "4       3      Third    G\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Merge with the Titanic DataFrame\n",
    "merged_df = pd.merge(df, class_info, on=\"Pclass\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify the merge\n",
    "print(\"Shape:\", merged_df.shape)\n",
    "print(\"\\nColumns:\")\n",
    "print(merged_df.columns)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Preview the new columns\n",
    "print(\"\\nPreview:\")\n",
    "print(merged_df[[\"Pclass\", \"class_name\", \"deck\"]].head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cdd0050e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 6 — Business question"
   ]
  },
